{"step_index":5285,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-23T16:14:07Z","thinking":"The user wants to eliminate randomness in the model's output by forcing a temperature setting of zero. The user is not using a direct API model, but is instead utilizing a custom request endpoint.\n\n\nMSEMAX utilizes the ChatGPT Web UI, making API-level `temperature` and `seed` settings ineffective, as the underlying web interface controls the sampling. The proposed \"fixed order\" for data storage doesn't apply because the files and storage configurations are dynamic, changing with different datasets. Therefore, a fixed order wouldn't be universally applicable.\n\n\nThe system must be robust to file order; real-world scenarios involve varying numbers of files with diverse names and warehouse assignments. Brand name similarity serves as a primary filter, moving beyond \"not found\" to a second level analyzing quantity, dosage, and other attributes. If the similarity algorithm is indecisive, the larger model will resolve the dosage discrepancies, but the name match moves the comparison to the second level.\n\n\nThe core principle focuses on a two-level hierarchy to eliminate false negatives. Level 1 ensures an item never returns \"not found\" if a brand match, exact or similar, exists in any storage. Level 2 then uses deterministic rules to classify the match. A direct match occurs if the brand and form are the same, even with differing quantities or prices.\n\n\nThe LLM's role is to resolve discrepancies in similar item names, particularly regarding concentration, size, or OCR complexities. If the LLM identifies a mismatch or expresses doubt, the item should be moved to \"Review,\" not \"Not Found.\" The current implementation incorrectly classifies candidates found in the warehouse but rejected by the LLM as \"Not Found.\" This leads to false negatives. The coordinator needs to be corrected to move LLM-rejected candidates to \"Review\" instead of \"Not Found.\"\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"d:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy\\src\\fast_match\\coordinator.py","EndLine":225,"StartLine":185,"toolAction":"Viewing coordinator candidate filter","toolSummary":"Inspect candidate routing in coordinator"}}]}
