{"step_index":5309,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-23T16:15:39Z","thinking":"The high brand similarity between the item and candidate suggests a strong match. However, the overall score is significantly lower because the system incorporates TF-IDF, which accounts for the differences in the complete item descriptions, leading to a reduced similarity score.\n\n\nSince the similarity score (0.617) fell below the auto-match threshold (0.88), the item was forwarded to the LLM. Unfortunately, the LLM in PROC-007 did not include the item in its JSON response, resulting in the item being categorized as \"not found.\" The user's feedback emphasizes that close brand names should elevate the item beyond the \"not found\" stage, prompting further analysis of dosage, quantity, and other attributes when the similarity algorithm is inconclusive.\n\n\nIf a brand match or plausible similarity exists, the item should be excluded from \"not found\" classification. 100% brand and form matches, regardless of quantity or packaging variations, warrant automatic code-level matching. Even with OCR typos or dosage ambiguities, the item should be routed to \"Review\" instead of \"not found\" if the LLM doesn't confirm an absolute match.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"d:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy\\src\\fast_match\\search.py","EndLine":180,"StartLine":80,"toolAction":"Viewing FastCandidateFinder implementation","toolSummary":"Check search.py candidate scoring"}}]}
{"step_index":5310,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-23T16:15:49Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-23T19:15:49+03:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-23T19:15:49+03:00\nFile Path: `file:///d:/AI_Engineer/Pharmacy-agy/src/fast_match/search.py`\nTotal Lines: 157\nTotal Bytes: 7093\nShowing lines 80 to 157\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n80:     text = re.sub(r'\\s+', ' ', text).strip()\n81:     return text\n82: \n83: class FastCandidateFinder:\n84:     def __init__(self):\n85:         # Character N-Grams (2 to 4 chars)\n86:         self.vectorizer = TfidfVectorizer(analyzer='char_wb', ngram_range=(2, 4))\n87:         self.corpus = []\n88:         self.original_names = []\n89:         self.ids = []\n90:         self.matrix = None\n91: \n92:     def fit(self, warehouse_items: list[dict]):\n93:         \"\"\"\n94:         warehouse_items: list of dicts with 'id' and 'name'\n95:         \"\"\"\n96:         self.ids = [item[\"id\"] for item in warehouse_items]\n97:         self.original_names = [item[\"name\"] for item in warehouse_items]\n98:         self.corpus = [normalize_for_search(name) for name in self.original_names]\n99:         \n100:         if self.corpus:\n101:             self.matrix = self.vectorizer.fit_transform(self.corpus)\n102: \n103:     def search(self, query: str, top_k: int = 6) -> list[dict]:\n104:         \"\"\"Returns the top_k most similar items from the warehouse with pharmaceutical validation.\"\"\"\n105:         if not self.corpus:\n106:             return []\n107:             \n108:         q_norm = normalize_for_search(query)\n109:         if not q_norm:\n110:             return []\n111:             \n112:         q_vec = self.vectorizer.transform([q_norm])\n113:         sims = cosine_similarity(q_vec, self.matrix).flatten()\n114:         \n115:         # Look at top candidates\n116:         top_indices = np.argsort(sims)[-top_k * 3:][::-1]\n117:         \n118:         req_brand = extract_brand_tokens(query)\n119:         req_form = extract_form_group(query)\n120:         \n121:         results = []\n122:         for idx in top_indices:\n123:             score = float(sims[idx])\n124:             cand_name = self.original_names[idx]\n125:             cand_brand = extract_brand_tokens(cand_name)\n126:             cand_form = extract_form_group(cand_name)\n127:             \n128:             # Rule 1: Zero tolerance for conflicting dosage forms (Tablets vs Syrup, Cream vs Suppository, etc.)\n129:             if req_form and cand_form and req_form != cand_form:\n130:                 continue\n131:                 \n132:             # Rule 2: Brand similarity check (Levenshtein / Token sort)\n133:             words_req = req_brand.split()\n134:             words_cand = cand_brand.split()\n135:             if len(words_req) > 1 or len(words_cand) > 1:\n136:                 brand_sim = fuzz.token_sort_ratio(req_brand, cand_brand)\n137:             else:\n138:                 brand_sim = fuzz.ratio(req_brand, cand_brand)\n139:                 \n140:             # Check prefix match for brand names\n141:             if req_brand and cand_brand:\n142:                 if req_brand.startswith(cand_brand) or cand_brand.startswith(req_brand):\n143:                     brand_sim = max(brand_sim, 80)\n144:                     \n145:             # Rule 3: Only accept candidates that share the brand name (>=58%) OR very high TF-IDF (>=0.50)\n146:             if brand_sim >= 58 or score >= 0.50:\n147:                 results.append({\n148:                     \"id\": self.ids[idx],\n149:                     \"name\": cand_name,\n150:                     \"score\": score,\n151:                     \"brand_sim\": brand_sim\n152:                 })\n153:                 if len(results) >= top_k:\n154:                     break\n155:                     \n156:         return results\n157: \nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
{"step_index":5311,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-23T16:15:49Z","thinking":"`FastCandidateFinder` identifies potential matches based on a threshold of brand similarity or score; these are candidates. Examining the coordinator logic, a high confidence rule triggers an auto-match, bypassing other steps if the best score and brand similarity meet a defined criteria.\n\n\nHigh-confidence TF-IDF matches are directly accepted. Plausible candidates identified via TF-IDF, but lacking high confidence, are passed to a language model for clinical rule evaluation. The coordinator processes LLM results, but \"no_match\" statuses are implicitly ignored, not explicitly handled. Final \"not found\" items are determined by subtracting matched and review-only names from the initial set.\n\n\nThe \"no_match\" status from the language model, or the omission of a match, incorrectly classifies candidates as \"not found\" even when potential matches exist. The core issue lies in how the coordinator handles language model responses; it implicitly ignores \"no_match\" statuses without re-evaluating the candidate. Therefore, items are incorrectly categorized as not found, despite having been identified as candidates.\n\n\nThe \"Not Found\" status should only be assigned if the initial search algorithm fails to locate any candidate or the brand similarity is below the threshold. Once a potential brand match is found, the item is removed from the \"Not Found\" category.\n\nA deterministic auto-match is triggered if brand names are identical or highly similar, the pharmaceutical form aligns (e.g., tablet vs. capsule), and the concentration either matches or is unspecified. Discrepancies in other attributes (quantity, packaging type) are tolerated within the auto-match criteria.\n\n\nDirect, deterministic matching rules are implemented.  Specific terms (e.g., \"باكو\", \"باكت 16\", company suffixes, and price indicators) trigger immediate 100% matches within the code, bypassing the language model for speed and certainty.  Discrepancies like \"زنكترون 30 كبسولة\" vs \"زنكترون أقراص باكت 160\" are now automatically matched.\n\nWhen there's brand similarity but differences in concentration, size, or OCR errors, the LLM is consulted. If the LLM validates the match, it becomes a \"match.\" Otherwise, the item goes to a \"review required\" status.\n\n\nA testing script is needed to validate the updated logic's effectiveness. The script will quantify the items auto-matched through the defined brand and form rules. It will also identify items that, due to having candidate matches, are correctly excluded from the \"not found\" category. The goal is to verify that no items with potential matches are incorrectly categorized as \"not found\" under the new rules.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":false,"Summary":"Test script for the proposed 3-level hierarchy","UserFacing":false},"CodeContent":"import sys\nsys.path.insert(0, \".\")\nfrom src.extract.excel_reader import read_excel, extract_item_names\nfrom src.extract.file_handler import read_input_files\nfrom src.fast_match.search import FastCandidateFinder\nfrom src.normalize.cleaner import extract_brand_tokens, extract_form_group, extract_strength\nfrom rapidfuzz import fuzz\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\n# Load shortages\ns_rows = read_excel(Path(\"data/processes/PROC-008/input_shortages/0913.xlsx\"))\nshortages = extract_item_names(s_rows)\nunique_shortages = {}\nfor s in shortages:\n    name = s[\"item_name_raw\"].strip()\n    if name and name not in unique_shortages:\n        unique_shortages[name] = s\n\n# Load warehouses\nwh_files = list(Path(\"data/processes/PROC-008/input_warehouses\").glob(\"*.*\"))\nfrom src.config import load_config\nconfig = load_config()\nwh_data = read_input_files(wh_files, role=\"warehouse\", api_key=config.unstructured_api_key)\n\nprint(f\"\\nUnique shortages: {len(unique_shortages)}\")\nprint(f\"Warehouses: {len(wh_data)}\")\n\n# Let's test the 8 controversial items under this logic\ntest_targets = [\n    \"سكينورين كريم\",\n    \"زنكترون 30كبسولة س ج\",\n    \"بالموكورت  25. مجم امبول س ج\",\n    \"كارنيفيتا ادفانس للرجال30كيس س ج\",\n    \"ب ك ميرز كبسول س ج\",\n    \"سينوبريل كواقراص س ج\",\n    \"تادالاندرو5جم30قرص\",\n    \"هيرو دي3+كي2 نقط\"\n]\n\nprint(\"\\n=== EVALUATION OF THE 8 ITEMS UNDER 3-LEVEL HIERARCHY ===\")\nfor target in test_targets:\n    target_brand = extract_brand_tokens(target)\n    target_form = extract_form_group(target)\n    target_str = extract_strength(target)\n    \n    found_candidates = []\n    for wh_name, wh_items in wh_data.items():\n        finder = FastCandidateFinder()\n        wh_catalog = [{\"id\": f\"W-{i:05}\", \"name\": it.get(\"item_name_raw\", \"\")} for i, it in enumerate(wh_items)]\n        finder.fit(wh_catalog)\n        cands = finder.search(target, top_k=3)\n        for c in cands:\n            found_candidates.append((wh_name, c[\"name\"], c[\"score\"], c.get(\"brand_sim\", 0)))\n            \n    found_candidates.sort(key=lambda x: (x[3], x[2]), reverse=True)\n    if found_candidates:\n        top = found_candidates[0]\n        cand_brand = extract_brand_tokens(top[1])\n        cand_form = extract_form_group(top[1])\n        cand_str = extract_strength(top[1])\n        print(f\"\\nالصنف: [{target}]\")\n        print(f\"   أفضل مرشح: [{top[1]}] في ({top[0]}) | BrandSim={top[3]:.1f}\")\n        print(f\"   تحليل: Target(brand={target_brand}, form={target_form}, str={target_str}) vs Cand(brand={cand_brand}, form={cand_form}, str={cand_str})\")\n        # Can it ever go to \"لم يتم العثور عليه\"?\n        print(f\"   -> النتيجة المنطقية: خرج تماماً من 'لم يتم العثور عليه'! إما مطابقة مباشرة أو مراجعة.\")\n    else:\n        print(f\"\\nالصنف: [{target}] -> لم يجد أي مرشح!\")\n","Description":"Test proposed 3-level hierarchy","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\kakak\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\916274de-7f92-49fc-a0a8-d291664b474a\\scratch\\test_hierarchy.py","toolAction":"Writing hierarchy test script","toolSummary":"Test 3-level hierarchy logic"}}]}
